 C/MI:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/MI - fix up the low half of a signed integer multiply.
C
C   Calling convention (single arg, in ACC):
C     ACC = the naive low half of the product (from KMUL/YTA)  ->  ACC = corrected
C     M13 = return link
C
C work.p2c's mcMULTI macro emits a call to this right after a KMUL whose
C result needs the signed low half rather than the unsigned one KYTA+64
C gives (genFullExpr's opfMULMSK case, and the negative-stride packed-array
C index case).  This is the Pascal runtime's P/MI (paslib/p_mi.dtran),
C ported instruction for instruction: [M1+13B] is MAXREAL (all ones
C without the sign bit) from libc/c_bx.madlen's constant table;
C XOR-AND-XOR through it replaces bits 7-47 of the naive value with
C YTA's non-logical reconstruction from Y, keeping the sign (bit 48)
C and the low 6 bits from the naive value.
C===========================================================
           15   ,ATX ,1      . [SP+1] := ACC, the naive low half
                ,YTA ,100B   . ACC := Y's mantissa, sign cleared, unshifted
           15   ,AEX ,1      . ACC ^= [SP+1]
            1   ,AAX ,13B    . ACC &= the positive-mantissa mask
           15   ,AEX ,1      . ACC ^= [SP+1]
           13   ,UJ  ,       . return the corrected low half
                ,END ,
